<Page title="Editorial and sourcing policy" eyebrow="Standards" description="How FBA Tactics decides what to publish: primary sources only, a claims register, independent checking, dated verification, corrections, and how the site is funded." updated="November 8, 2026" lede="The rules every page on this site follows. If you find a page that breaks one, tell us and we will fix it publicly.">
  <h2>1. Primary sources only</h2>
  <p>A fact may be published only if it comes from the body that issues it: a regulation (eCFR), a Federal Register notice, an IRS publication, or a marketplace's own public fee or policy page. Blogs, software vendors, agencies, forums, news summaries, wikis and AI-generated sites are not cited, even when they are right. If a reader cannot open the source without logging in, we do not rely on it.</p>
  <h2>2. Every fact is registered</h2>
  <p>Each factual sentence is linked to an entry in a claims register that records the claim, the source address, the publisher, the date it was opened, a short excerpt proving it, who drafted it and who checked it. The site's build refuses to publish a page that cites an unchecked entry.</p>
  <h2>3. Separate checking</h2>
  <p>The pass that checks a page is separate from the pass that drafted it. The checker reopens each source and confirms the number, date and scope match. Statements that fail are corrected from a primary source or removed.</p>
  <h2>4. Dates on everything that changes</h2>
  <p>Pages show when they were published, updated and last verified. Every source line shows the date it was checked. We do not change dates without rechecking the content.</p>
  <h2>5. No invented anything</h2>
  <p>No fictional experts, quotes, testimonials, case studies, statistics or claims of having tested products. Worked examples use hypothetical inputs and say so. Charts plot only sourced numbers on honest axes.</p>
  <h2>6. How pages are made</h2>
  <p>Pages are researched and drafted with the help of AI writing tools working from the primary sources, then checked against those sources as described above. The publisher is responsible for every page.</p>
  <h2>7. Funding and independence</h2>
  <p>The site is intended to be funded by display advertising from Google AdSense. Advertisers have no say in what is written. Ads are labeled, kept out of tables, calculators, navigation and source lists, and never made to look like content. There are no affiliate links, sponsored posts or paid placements. Platforms and agencies named here have not paid for or reviewed coverage.</p>
  <h2>8. Images</h2>
  <p>Charts, diagrams and page graphics are drawn by the site from sourced data. Screenshots of seller dashboards and third-party logos are not used. See <a href="/image-credits/">image credits</a>.</p>
  <h2>9. Corrections</h2>
  <p>Errors are corrected promptly and logged with the date and what changed on the <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>. Silent edits to a published figure are not allowed.</p>
  <h2>10. Retired pages</h2>
  <p>In November 2026 the site withdrew guides whose figures could not be traced to primary sources. Where a verified page covers the same question, the old address forwards to it; otherwise it returns "not found". A withdrawn guide returns only after it passes the checks above.</p>
</Page>
